<h2>Asobi Review 0.2 (build 479)</h2>
<p><b>The command line answers in the spelling you typed.</b></p>
<ul>
<li><b><code>Asobi optimize</code> is now the documented spelling</b>, and its help says so. Both spellings have always run — but typing <code>optimize</code> printed help that told you to type <code>optimise</code>, and offered <code>--input &lt;colour space&gt;</code>. <code>optimise</code> stays a working alias, so any script or render-farm job already written against it keeps running untouched.</li>
<li>The encode-failure message reads "Optimize failed" rather than "Optimise failed", which is what the same error already said on the other path.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
